    docs: retire the reconciliation_delta aggregation plan (Phase 4e) (#19)
    
    Real trading-main ledger data (momentum's 17 consecutive trade_close events,
    my-crypto's one valid data point) shows reconciliation_delta is exactly
    -(entry_fee + exit_fee) every single time -- exchange_profit is reported
    gross-of-fees, net_pnl is fee-deducted, so the two will always differ by
    exactly the fees. It's not noise around a real signal; it's a known, benign,
    always-same-direction artifact that no aggregation window would ever turn
    into a meaningful "something is systematically wrong" alarm.
    
    The problem this metric was originally meant to catch (local entry/exit price
    drifting from exchange reality, compounding into future stop-loss sizing) was
    already closed at the source by my-crypto's 2026-08-22 fix that records
    exchange-confirmed fill prices instead of estimates -- which is also why zero
    outlier deltas have ever been observed.
    
    §4.5/4.6/4.7 updated to reflect the retraction: reconciliation_delta stays a
    permanent event-log-only measurement, never feeds the error request queue.
    
    Co-authored-by: bcup02 <columnbb@gmail.com>
    Co-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

